I've added a //go:generate comment to the main.go file. The file now looks like this:

```go
//go:generate command-to-run

package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    fmt.Println("Hello, World!")
}
```

You can replace "command-to-run" with the actual command you want to use for code generation. This directive will be recognized by the 'go generate' tool when you run it.

